  "description": "Got an idea that's outgrown your notes app? A problem you can't stop poking at? Enigma's your excuse to finally build the thing. Two days. One online qualifier, one offline finale. Teams will ideate, build, and pitch their way from spark to shippable product - fuelled by instinct, iteration, and the occasional 2 AM breakthrough. No fixed theme, no predictable brief, just a problem worth solving and a clock that's always ticking. Enigma isn't about who codes the fastest. It's about who builds the smartest. Guidelines: Undergraduate college students from all across India are eligible Cross-college participation is allowed Multiple teams from the same college are allowed to participate The final round will be conducted at the IIM Indore campus Participants must adhere to all event rules and guidelines The team will reach out to the participants with detailed rules post-registration The competition is exclusively for Undergraduate Students Note: Candidates shortlisted for the offline rounds are required to confirm their participation by registering through the link that will be shared via email by participation_atharvranbhoomi@iimidr.ac.in. Failure to register through the said link will result in your entry not being counted for Atharv Ranbhoomi 2026. Further details will be intimated via the same channel for the shortlisted teams.",
